= The CEDA Enters the Government

President Alcalá-Zamora gives way at last: three CEDA ministers enter Lerroux's cabinet. To the right it is normal parliamentary arithmetic - the largest party takes its place in government. To the left it is 1922 all over again, the moment Mussolini was let in the door, and the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT**</span> have sworn for a year that they would answer it with a general strike.

Now the threat must be made good or abandoned. The revolutionary committees issue the call. In most of Spain the rising will sputter and fail within a day - but in Asturias, and in Barcelona, it will not.

[? if left_dissent >= 40 : There is no holding our base back now; the order to rise has been given. ?]
